{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/324913731465542/posts/1080016372621937/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/324913731465542/posts/1080016372621937/","title":"Loveland Politics | **What does the science say about 5G | Facebook","description":"**What does the science say about 5G?\n\n**Yale Neurologist Steve Novella on *Science-Based Medicine*\n\n","language":"en","text":"## Loveland Politics Join\n\nJoin\n\nWhat does the science say about 5G technology?\n\nTitles are generated by AI from Meta\n\n1\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nShare\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nGeorge Garklavs\n\nThere will always be people who, on hearing about speculative hazard, turn it into real, known, 100% guaranteed proof positive of some danger. They will simply ignore the speculative nature of the \"hazard\" or the fact that some odd finding is not reproduceable.\n\n3","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":1613.1072999996832,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}